      "moderator_questions": [
        {
          "id": "mq1",
          "sw": "Swali 1: Nambari na ngeli",
          "en": "Question 1: Numbers and noun classes",
          "body": {
            "sw": "Katika Kiswahili 'watu wawili' lakini 'vitabu viwili' — neno 'wawili/viwili' linabadilika kulingana na ngeli. Katika Kiingereza 'two' haibadiliki kamwe. Katika lugha yako — nambari inabadilika kulingana na kitu au daima ni sawa?",
            "en": "In Swahili 'watu wawili' (two people) but 'vitabu viwili' (two books) — the word 'two' changes according to noun class. In English 'two' never changes. In your language — does the number change depending on the object or always stay the same?"
          },
          "options": {
            "sw": [
              "Ni sawa — nambari haibadiliki",
              "Inabadilika → toa mifano na vitu tofauti na tafsiri"
            ],
            "en": [
              "Always the same — numbers do not change",
              "Changes → give examples with different objects and translations"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "mq2",
          "sw": "Swali 2: Maumbo maalum ya 1 na 2",
          "en": "Question 2: Special forms for 1 and 2",
          "body": {
            "sw": "Katika baadhi ya lugha nambari 1 na 2 zina maumbo maalum — zinapatana na nomino tofauti na nambari nyingine. Kwa mfano katika Kirusi nambari 1 na 2 zinabadilika kulingana na jinsia. Katika lugha yako — nambari 1 na 2 zina maalum au zinafanya kazi kama nyingine zote?",
            "en": "In some languages numbers 1 and 2 have special forms — they agree with nouns differently from other numbers. In Russian numbers 1 and 2 change by gender. In your language — do numbers 1 and 2 have special forms or work like all other numbers?"
          },
          "options": {
            "sw": [
              "Zinafanya kazi kama nyingine zote",
              "Zina maalum → toa mifano na tafsiri"
            ],
            "en": [
              "Same as all other numbers",
              "Special forms exist → give examples and translations"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "mq3",
          "sw": "Swali 3: Kukusanya kitabu cha sarufi",
          "en": "Question 3: Building the grammar reference",
          "body": {
            "sw": "Kulingana na maudhui yote — maneno, misemo ya wasemaji na majibu ya maswali — tunga kitabu kifupi cha sarufi kuhusu mada hii katika lugha yako.",
            "en": "Based on all content provided — words, speakers' phrases and answers to the questions — write a short grammar reference on this topic in your language."
          },
          "structure": {
            "sw": [
              "Salamu — orodha kamili na maelezo ni lini kutumia",
              "Kuaga — orodha kamili",
              "Maneno ya heshima na majibu yake",
              "Nambari — je, zinapatana na ngeli, maumbo maalum ya 1 na 2",
              "Siku za juma — maneno yake au ya mpangilio",
              "Miezi — majina yake au ya kukopa",
              "Jinsi ya kusema wakati — saa, dakika, nyakati za siku"
            ],
            "en": [
              "Greetings — full list with notes on when to use each",
              "Farewells — full list",
              "Polite expressions and responses",
              "Numbers — agreement with classes, special forms for 1 and 2",
              "Days of the week — own words or ordinal",
              "Months — own names or borrowed",
              "How to express time — hours, minutes, parts of the day"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
